type: software
title: "Constructing oriented hierarchies: Python implementations"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Andrianarivony
    given-names: Fidy Heritiana
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5371-3262"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Fidy-Heritiana/A-fast-algorithm-for-constructing-an-oriented-hierarchy"
url: "https://github.com/Fidy-Heritiana/A-fast-algorithm-for-constructing-an-oriented-hierarchy"
abstract: >-
  Python research code for constructing oriented hierarchies from binary data
  in Statistical Implicative Analysis. The repository provides a construction
  method using a heap and graph traversal, an optimized comparison method,
  example datasets and execution instructions. The documentation records the
  default scoring and threshold conventions used by the two implementations.
keywords:
  - oriented hierarchies
  - statistical implicative analysis
  - algorithm analysis
  - greedy algorithms
  - graph algorithms
  - Python
